KZ3 patch 1098 (SPU pass 73): lift-time guesses for computed hops between lifted SPU functions.

Software-pipelined SPU loops close with `bi rX`, rX = selb(head, exit, cond), the head loaded by `ila` before the
loop (KZ3's audio mixer jobs: 0xD100 -> 0xD2DC -> 0xD100 ...). Since patch 1096 every such hop went through
spu_ib_direct: an out-of-line call, the lookup memo's hash and load, the registry load and an indirect jump, 9.9 %
of the audio SPU thread (SPU pass 72 profile).
- tools/spu_lifter.py compute_ib_guesses: from each computed-hop site, scan back in address order for the target
  register's writer, following selb (both value operands) and copies down to il/ila constants that start a lifted
  function of the image (at most two per site; never the runtime's special addresses). Such sites emit
  SPU_IB_HOP_G(ctx, T, SPU_IB_GUESS(ctx, G, F) ...); the TU registers its guesses after its functions
  (spu_ib_guess_register) and keeps its image id in s_spu_ib_gid only when spu_lookup(G, id) is F for each.
- spu_context.h: SPU_IB_GUESS tail-calls F directly when the target is G and spu_ib_guess_ok() holds: each of
  spu_ib_direct's tests for that constant, the same or stricter, and an image test in place of the lookup (the
  resident overlay is the TU's image, or there is none and the context's image is), so a guess hop runs exactly
  what spu_ib_direct would have returned; any other case takes the old path.
KZ3_SPU_IBGUESS=0 = old path (same exe); KZ3_HOP_STATS=1 adds `guess=` (guess hops per 10 s) to [hop-stats].
Needs a relift. Upstream candidate (with 1096).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): both.

